;; Package a64i is arm64's machine on Arbace's emulator frame (doc/asm/ARM64-SURVEY.md §4.2, AR5; the frame go/arbace/emu,
;; SH5): A64's integer core (data processing, branches, loads and stores, exclusives and LSE atomics, the system
;; instructions a user program meets) run at user level, Linux's system calls by name. Two inputs, one machine: an
;; instruction comes from the decoder (Decode: the linked bytes, AOT) or from its assembly form (FromForm: the forms laid
;; out, eval), both giving an Inst, the one execution's input. The semantics are written from the Arm ARM's pseudocode
;; (DDI 0487), by Arbace; no code copied.
(in-ns 'go.arbace.a64i) (go/file "inst.go" :doc "Package a64i is arm64's machine on Arbace's emulator frame (doc/asm/ARM64-SURVEY.md §4.2, AR5; the frame go/arbace/emu,\nSH5): A64's integer core (data processing, branches, loads and stores, exclusives and LSE atomics, the system\ninstructions a user program meets) run at user level, Linux's system calls by name. Two inputs, one machine: an\ninstruction comes from the decoder (Decode: the linked bytes, AOT) or from its assembly form (FromForm: the forms laid\nout, eval), both giving an Inst, the one execution's input. The semantics are written from the Arm ARM's pseudocode\n(DDI 0487), by Arbace; no code copied.\n" :imports [

    ^{:line 9} [fmt "fmt"]])


